review:
Very ambitious and somewhat underrated open-world FPS set in an undisclosed East African country engulfed in civil war. Not everyone will appreciate its immersive world and some unique elements or its depiction of a senseless and unnecessary war. If you like a gritty atmosphere and can accept or modify some frustrating features, give it a try.

Pros:
- Amazing visuals;
- Decent stealth (can be improved with mods);
- Great environmental storytelling;
- Good gunplay;
- Great optimisation;
- Interesting "villain";
- Atmospheric environment and gameplay elements;
- Great sound design and soundtrack;
- Responsive controls;
- Great attention to detail;
- Awesome arsenal;
- Decent modding community;
- Good voice acting, but many lines spoken too quickly;
- Cool fire mechanics;
- Decent AI;

Cons:
- Too much driving;
- Convoluted story;
- Towards the second half, the gameplay loop becomes quite tedious;
- Enemies in outposts respawn too quickly (can be fixed with mods);
- Repetitive mission design;
